        "heading": "We started <em>with the water.</em>",
        "lead": "<p>You choose your soap, your shampoo, your towels with care. The water running over all of it rarely gets a thought.</p>",
        "text": "<p>Then you start to notice it. The smell of chlorine on a hot morning shower. The film of sediment that builds up on the glass. It is added to keep tap water safe to drink, and it is still there when you step into the shower.</p><p>We looked for a filter that fixed that, and found mostly bulky plastic that hid its cartridge and looked like hardware. So we designed one we would want on display: a clear handle that lets you see the filter at work, a chrome head, and nothing you have to hide.</p><p>Inside, water passes through two stages. A PP cotton filter catches sediment and fine particles. Then a calcium sulfite cartridge helps reduce chlorine. Both are replaceable in minutes, with no tools and no plumber.</p><p>The result is a simple ritual, made a little more comfortable.</p>",
        "show_image": true,
